description: Decisions now start as git-issue issues (closed, `issue_type: decision`), but DECISIONS.md is still edited by hand, so the two drift and both lanes draw D-numbers from one sequence. #78 hit that: eight llvm decisions reused numbers main held (D206-D212, D217) and had to be renumbered to D235-D242.
 
 I'd add a checks/ script that renders DECISIONS.md from the closed decision issues, ordered by date, each entry keyed by its D-number (`external_ref`) and citing its issue id, with a `workflow.mk` target to regenerate it and a check that the committed file matches. New decisions then take their number when the file is generated, not when someone writes it, so two branches cannot pick the same one. D1-D205 have no issues yet; they would be imported first, or kept as a fixed preamble the script leaves alone.
 
 This is the same move git-issue:562dff4 proposes for STATUS.md, and it settles git-issue:2a446d9's README wording. DECISIONS.md is yours to maintain, so the format and whether to adopt it are your call.

## Comments
[2026-10-28T06:24:52Z] Matt Parrett: Adopted, with D1 to D205 as a fixed preamble the script leaves alone. From D206 on, DECISIONS.md is rendered from the closed decision issues, ordered by date, each entry keyed by its D-number in `external_ref` and citing its issue id, and the committed file must match the render. Entries keep the current heading shape so every existing citation still resolves. Two details to settle before the script is written. First, numbering: a PR cites its decision in code and in its title before it merges, so the number has to exist before the render; I'd have the decision issue take `external_ref` when it is created (one past the highest on the fetched board) and let the drift check fail on a duplicate, which keeps the collision window to the gap between two unpushed creations. If you would rather numbers come only from the render, the PRs cite the issue id until merge and the render rewrites nothing, so say which. Second, the wasm lane's D230 to D234 have work issues but no decision issues; I will file those five before the switch so the first render covers main as it stands. The script, the workflow.mk target and the check are yours if you want them with the STATUS.md one from the related proposal; otherwise this lane takes them after its open PRs land.
